{
  "dom_id": "step-q87760",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14178864/assets/7c1663caeea9751ccbaa2544792c9c15331accedc6dd757b44154673f34f8ddc.png)\n\nWhat is a correct congruence statement for the quadrilaterals shown in the diagram above?",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that $∠M≅∠O.$ \n\nLet's determine the vertices in the second quadrilateral that correspond to $M.$ First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}MN & =DE \\\\ MP & =DG \\\\ ∠M & ≅∠D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- vertex $M$ corresponds to vertex $D,$\n\n- consequently, vertex $O$ corresponds to vertex $F.$\n\nAs for the other two vertices, notice we have two more pairs of congruent angles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠N & ≅∠E \\\\ ∠P & ≅∠G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have two more pairs of congruent sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}OP & =FG \\\\ ON & =FE,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n- vertex $N$ corresponds to $E,$ and\n\n- vertex $P$ corresponds to $G.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that a correct congruence statement is\n\n$$\nMNOP≅DEFG.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
